{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979989028,"sessionID":"ses_1cc881df1ffe8Nr2Z3qy4C9Ok7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_V1fh7m63KTOTgBgojb9x11pD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":34190,"limit":80},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n34190: \n34191: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11146428\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32424507\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047036 \"A smooth muscle cell located in the middle layer of the muscularis externa of the stomach wall. This cell is arranged concentrically with the stomach's longitudinal axis, forming a continuous sheet of contractile tissue. It is fusiform in shape, containing actin and myosin filaments that enable contraction without striations. This cell contributes to the mechanical digestion and movement of food within the stomach through coordinated contractions, and plays a role in forming the pyloric sphincter in the pyloric region.\")\n34192: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047036 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34193: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047036 \"2024-12-09T10:40:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34194: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047036 \"stomach smooth muscle circular layer cell\"@en)\n34195: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047036 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000192 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008857)))\n34196: \n34197: # Class: obo:CL_4047037 (stomach smooth muscle inner oblique layer cell)\n34198: \n34199: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29493959\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047037 \"A smooth muscle cell found in the innermost layer of the muscularis externa of the stomach wall. This cell forms a unique layer of smooth muscle fibers oriented obliquely to the stomach's longitudinal axis. It is responsible for aiding in the mixing and churning of gastric contents, contributing to mechanical digestion within the stomach.\")\n34200: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047037 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34201: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047037 \"2024-12-09T10:53:19Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34202: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4047037 \"stomach smooth muscle oblique layer cell\")\n34203: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047037 \"stomach smooth muscle inner oblique layer cell\"@en)\n34204: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047037 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000192 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008862)))\n34205: \n34206: # Class: obo:CL_4047038 (dogiel type I neuron)\n34207: \n34208: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1038/s41575-020-0271-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1038/s41575-021-00561-y\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32152479\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047038 \"A multipolar neuron in the myenteric plexus of the gastrointestinal tract, characterized by a small to medium-sized cell body and multiple short dendrites.  This neuron exhibits fast excitatory postsynaptic potentials and can be classified into stubby, spiny and hairy subtypes based on dendritic morphology. (Brehmer, 2021)\")\n34209: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047038 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34210: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047038 \"2024-12-16T13:42:04Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34211: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047038 \"dogiel type I neuron\")\n34212: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047038 obo:CL_0000104)\n34213: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047038 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002439))\n34214: \n34215: # Class: obo:CL_4047040 (smooth muscle circular layer cell)\n34216: \n34217: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18221249\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27445346\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047040 \"A smooth muscle cell that is found in the inner muscular layer of hollow organs. It is characterized by its spiral/helical arrangement around organ lumens. This cell is crucial for peristaltic movements in organs.\")\n34218: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047040 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34219: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047040 \"2025-01-06T15:40:21Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34220: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047040 \"smooth muscle circular layer cell\")\n34221: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047040 obo:CL_0000192)\n34222: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047040 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0012368))\n34223: \n34224: # Class: obo:CL_4047042 (type 1 myenteric plexus glia)\n34225: \n34226: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19906678\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21865647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26964064\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28066889\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047042 \"An enteric glial cell located within the myenteric ganglia of the gastrointestinal tract. This cell has a small somata and has very short, irregularly branched processes that surround neuron cell bodies, giving it a protoplasmic-like appearance. It plays crucial roles in modulating myenteric neuron activity, regulating oxidative stress, and influencing neuroinflammation and neurogenesis.\")\n34227: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047042 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34228: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047042 \"2025-02-10T16:49:55Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34229: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4047042 \"type 1 MP\")\n34230: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047042 \"type 1 myenteric plexus glia\")\n34231: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047042 obo:CL_4040002)\n34232: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047042 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002439))\n34233: \n34234: # Class: obo:CL_4047043 (type 1 submucosal plexus glia)\n34235: \n34236: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.3389/fncel.2023.1170309\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28487635\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047043 \"An enteric glial cell that is associated with neuron cell bodies within submucosal ganglia of the gastrointestinal tract. This cell is located in the submucosa, a layer of connective tissue beneath the intestinal mucosa. This cell plays a role in modulating secretomotor neuron activity and contributes to the regulation of digestive fluid secretion and absorption.\")\n34237: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047043 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34238: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047043 \"2025-02-10T17:02:28Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34239: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4047043 \"type I SMP\")\n34240: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047043 \"type 1 submucosal plexus glia\")\n34241: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047043 obo:CL_4040002)\n34242: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047043 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0009566))\n34243: \n34244: # Class: obo:CL_4047044 (type 2 interganglionic glia)\n34245: \n34246: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1002/glia.22876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35111752\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047044 \"An enteric glial cell that has an elongated, fibrous morphology with long processes that run parallel to nerve fibers connecting enteric myenteric ganglia. This cell is located in the interganglionic fiber tracts of the enteric nervous system.\")\n34247: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047044 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34248: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047044 \"2025-02-11T12:28:37Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34249: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35111752\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4047044 \"type II enteric glia\")\n34250: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047044 \"type 2 interganglionic glia\")\n34251: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047044 obo:CL_4040002)\n34252: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047044 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000429))\n34253: \n34254: # Class: obo:CL_4047045 (type 3 mucosal glia)\n34255: \n34256: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25161129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37153631\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38957473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047045 \"An enteric glial cell located in the lamina propria of the intestinal mucosa. This cell plays important roles in maintaining gut barrier function, regulating intestinal homeostasis, and mediating interactions between the enteric nervous system and the immune system.\")\n34257: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047045 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34258: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047045 \"2025-02-11T12:39:11Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34259: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047045 \"type 3 mucosal glia\")\n34260: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047045 obo:CL_4040002)\n34261: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4047045 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000030))\n34262: \n34263: # Class: obo:CL_4047047 (type I enteric glial cell)\n34264: \n34265: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/j.celrep.2023.112194\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29927320\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35111752\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047047 \"An enteric glial cell located within the ganglia of the enteric nervous system. This cell is characterized by it’s small somata and short, irregularly branched processes that surround neuronal cell bodies in the myenteric and submucosal ganglia. This cell plays important roles in modulating neuronal activity and neurogenesis in the gastrointestinal tract.\")\n34266: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047047 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\n34267: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047047 \"2025-02-11T13:35:14Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n34268: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4047047 \"intraganglionic glia\")\n34269: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4047047 \"type 1 enteric glia\")\n\n(Showing lines 34190-34269 of 35817. Use offset=34270 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11146428\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32424507\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047036 \"A smooth muscle cell located in the middle layer of the muscularis externa of the stomach wall. This cell is arranged concentrically with the stomach's longitudinal axis, forming a continuous sheet of contractile tissue. It is fusiform in shape, containing actin and myosin filaments that enable contraction without striations. This cell contributes to the mechanical digestion and movement of food within the stomach through coordinated contractions, and plays a role in forming the pyloric sphincter in the pyloric region.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4047036 <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7919-4905>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4047036 \"2024-12-09T10:40:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047036 \"stomach smooth muscle circular layer cell\"@en)\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047036 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000192 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008857)))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4047037 (stomach smooth muscle inner oblique layer cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29493959\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_404