{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980442495,"sessionID":"ses_1cc881df1ffe8Nr2Z3qy4C9Ok7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_kEq7RavP0CNlHdlfsdxvHno2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Added 14 new myenteric neuron terms requested in issue #3584 to `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+Summary of changes:\n+- Added `dogiel type II neuron` as a new general morphological neuron class.\n+- Added myenteric intrinsic primary afferent, interneuron, secretomotor/vasodilator, and intestinofugal neuron terms.\n+- Added ascending and descending interneuron subclasses of the new myenteric interneuron term.\n+- Added stubby and spiny Dogiel type I neuron classes for myenteric motor neuron morphotypes.\n+- Added `dogiel type II neuron of myenteric plexus` plus calretinin-positive and calretinin-negative IPAN subclasses.\n+- Added grouping classes for `cholinergic neuron of myenteric plexus` and `nitrergic neuron of myenteric plexus`.\n+\n+Modeling rationale:\n+- Followed existing enteric neuron patterns already present in the ontology, especially the local `dogiel type I neuron` term and existing use of `RO:0002100` with `UBERON:0002439` for myenteric plexus location.\n+- Used equivalence axioms where the issue supplied a clean genus-differentia pattern that could be expressed with entities already present in the ontology.\n+- Kept some requested biological detail in textual definitions rather than adding more aggressive logical axioms when the issue itself indicated missing imports or future refinement needs, such as calretinin protein expression and more specific neurotransmission GO terms.\n+- Added issue-tracker links and new-term metadata (`terms:date`, `terms:creator`) for each new class.\n+\n+Checks completed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Checked existing parent terms and local enteric neuron patterns in `sr